The full report is free to read, and the questionnaire is yours to reuse.

The survey grew out of our [order-to-cash review](/projects/order-to-cash-review/), where one finding came up again and again: the slowest step is rarely the one people blame.

We asked 120 owner-led businesses how their working week was spent. The companies ranged from ten to two hundred employees, and they worked in trade, manufacturing, logistics and professional services. We asked about meetings, approvals, rework and waiting time. The owners estimated each answer, and then we checked the estimates against a sample week.

## What we found

- Owners spent about a fifth of their week on approvals that rarely changed the outcome.
- Rework, such as correcting quotes or re-entering orders, took more time than anyone expected.
- Waiting for information from another team was the most common reason for a late delivery.

## What we are doing next

We will repeat the survey in 2027, and we are adding questions about hiring and training. If you run a business with between ten and two hundred people, you are welcome to answer the questionnaire too.
